  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 8203.01 Activation Criteria",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 8203.01 Activation Criteria.\n\n(a) A blue alert shall be implemented when:\n\n(1) In the line of duty, a law enforcement officer has been killed, injured, or is missing;\n\n(2) There is sufficient information available regarding the law enforcement officer's last known location; or\n\n(3) There is physical description of an offender or vehicle involved; and\n\n(4) The law enforcement agency determines that a public notification may aid in:\n\na. Apprehending a suspected offender who poses an imminent threat to the public or law enforcement personnel; or\n\nb. Locating the missing law enforcement officer.\n\nSource. #13298, eff 11-30-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c8200.html"
}
